{
  "format": "stock-ledger-v1",
  "about": "Golden vectors for the ledger -> stock-core bridge of the native apps (data/StockLedger.kt, run by StockLedgerVectorsTest on Android and desktop CI). The ledger uses the shape every app version already writes (web localStorage 'tohid-shop-data-v1' = Kotlin ShopData) plus the optional additive fields listed in the bridge header. Expected numbers were worked out by hand from the rules below and from stock-v1.json, not copied from either engine.",
  "rules": [
    "Events: warehouseEntries (receipt when !isAdjustment && units > 0, else an adjustment typed by adjKind / the supplier_return stock movement with the same refId / notes starting with 'انبارگردانی' = count), stockMovements of type 'transfer' (zero-sum, needs toLocationId), saleItems of sales that are not cancelled (orphan items count), returns capped by saleItem.returnedQty with the remainder at the sale time.",
    "Order: at (createdAt, else UTC midnight of date, else 1), then entry < transfer < sale < return, then id (UTF-16 order).",
    "Receipt cost = round(units * price * 100) minor + round(landedCost * 100) landed. Lot = batch, else 'w:'+entryId when it has a date, else none.",
    "History is replayed in recorded mode with today = the event's own day; a sale is split over locations: the scanned lot's location, the sale's location, then others by name; healthy stock first, then expired, then the shortage on the sale's location.",
    "On-hand per product (sum of locations) equals today's engine: sum(units) - sum(quantity - returnedQty) of non-cancelled sales.",
    "New work is checked in local mode: more than the healthy stock of the whole shop is refused (expired_stock when only expired units are missing).",
    "Setting: the latest auditLog row of type stock_mode (createdAt, then id) decides; refId 'on' = on; no row = off."
  ],
  "ledger": {
